{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Done.\n\nChanged:\n- `in/db/migration.sql`\n- `in/db/preflight_report.md`\n- `in/db/rollback.sql`\n- `in/db/postcheck.sql`\n- `in/db/migration_report.md`\n\nWhat changed:\n- Replaced destructive `DROP TABLE users` draft with an explicit offline SQLite transaction that rebuilds `users` and `orders`, copies all rows forward, preserves `created_at`, preserves `orders.user_id`, adds `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`, and enforces `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` plus `CHECK (trim(email) <> '')`.\n- Dirty-email cleanup is deterministic and id-based:\n  - `u4` → `ada+u4@example.com`\n  - `u5` → `missing+u5@example.invalid`\n  - `u6` → `missing+u6@example.invalid`\n- `rollback.sql` restores the old `users` shape: `id, email, name, created_at`, and rebuilds `orders` so the FK points back to restored `users`.\n- `postcheck.sql` verifies counts, dependent dirty-user orders, cleaned emails, preserved timestamps, constraints, and FK integrity.\n- Reports document preflight issues and migration/rollback behavior.\n\nVerification:\n- Executed `schema.sql`, then `migration.sql`, then `migration.sql` again, then `postcheck.sql`, then `rollback.sql` against a temp SQLite DB using Python’s built-in `sqlite3` module.\n- Observed after first migration:\n  - users: 6\n  - orders: 4\n  - dirty-user order refs preserved:\n    - `o2 -> u4`\n    - `o3 -> u5`\n    - `o4 -> u6`\n  - cleaned emails exactly matched required values.\n- Observed after second migration:\n  - same 6 user rows, same 4 order rows\n  - same cleaned emails\n  - `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` returned no rows.\n- Observed after rollback:\n  - `PRAGMA table_info(users)` shows columns `id, email, name, created_at`\n  - 6 user rows preserved\n  - 4 order rows preserved\n  - `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` returned no rows.\n\nKnown rollback behavior:\n- Rollback restores pre-migration schema shape, not original dirty email values. Cleaned emails remain. This is documented in `in/db/migration_report.md`."}}
