{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SQLite migration draft at `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/migration.sql` is unsafe. It loses data while trying to add account status and email constraints.\n\nRead `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md` before editing. It defines the required dirty-data cleanup, dependent order preservation, transaction, idempotency, and rollback expectations.\n\nYour job:\n- Edit only `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/migration.sql`.\n- Do not edit `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/schema.sql` or `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md`.\n- Preserve all existing users from `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/schema.sql`.\n- Preserve all existing orders and their `user_id` references.\n- Add a non-null `status` column with default `active`.\n- Enforce unique, non-null email addresses for future writes.\n- Keep historical `created_at` values.\n- Existing dirty rows include duplicate, null, and blank emails. Preserve those users by assigning deterministic migrated email values, and document the cleanup.\n- Also create `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md` describing duplicate/null email issues before migration.\n- The preflight report must also mention dependent orders for dirty users `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`.\n- Also create `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql` that can restore the pre-migration schema shape with id, email, name, created_at.\n- The rollback script must be executable after the migration and must restore the old schema shape.\n- Also create `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql` with verification queries that can be executed after the migration. It must check row counts, dependent order preservation, cleaned dirty-user emails, and email/status constraints.\n- Also create `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/038-043-db-migration-safety-omp-a01-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260831-112201-067e59f4/workspace/in/db/migration_report.md` summarizing the migration strategy, dirty-data cleanup, idempotency approach, rollback limitation/behavior, and the postcheck queries to run.\n- The migration should run inside an explicit transaction and should be idempotent: running it a second time must not corrupt or duplicate user data.\n- Use deterministic cleanup values exactly: duplicate `u4` becomes `ada+u4@example.com`; null email `u5` becomes `missing+u5@example.invalid`; blank email `u6` becomes `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n\nThe migration must run offline in SQLite. Do not use external tools or services.\n"}],"attribution":"user","timestamp":1788189722807},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","